course: dictionary
lesson: 6396
title: A small deer that barks
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A muntjac is a small deer. You may not know the word, but the words around it give clues. «The muntjac, a small deer from China, escaped from parks» tells you what kind of animal it is, and where it came from.
explain: Read on for more clues. «The little muntjac that barks like a dog in English woods at night» tells you that a muntjac makes a sound like a bark. That is why it is also called a barking deer.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does «a small deer that barks» still make sense? Yes, so you have understood the word.
fact: A muntjac is a small deer from Asia, also called a barking deer.
fact: Muntjacs make a loud bark, a bit like a dog.
fact: Male muntjacs have short antlers and long, tusk-like teeth.
fact: «Six kinds of deer live wild in Britain»: red and roe are native, and muntjac was brought by people.
fact: Muntjacs have spread wild in parts of England, not in every part.
exercise: «The muntjac is a small deer from Asia.» What is a muntjac? | A kind of fish | *A small deer | A type of tree | A large bird
exercise: Why is the muntjac also called a barking deer? | Because it has no voice at all | Because it is very quiet | *Because it makes a loud bark | Because it lives in the sea
exercise: «The muntjac, a small deer from China, escaped from parks.» Find and copy the word that tells you where it came from. | small | escaped | deer | *China
test: «The muntjac, a small deer from China, escaped from parks into the English countryside.» Where did muntjacs escape from first? | *From parks | From a desert | From deep caves | From the sea
test: Male muntjacs have short antlers and long, tusk-like teeth. What do the teeth look like? | Like flowers | Like long tails | *Like tusks | Like wings
exam: Which sentence about the muntjac is true? | *It is a small deer from Asia that can bark | It is a kind of tree that grows in parks | It is the biggest deer in the world | It is a large bird from Africa
